35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Shizue, I found that every room closed for works forces us to pay for off-site space for two terms.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: @Yumi, that’s a heavy cost. I found our technicians are stuck doing manual checks because the current extraction gear can’t handle it alone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"-Mizuki: @George, that sounds exhausting. I found that projects rated highest were those anyone could book, not just one wing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, that aligns with my findings. Tender prices for mechanical plant have risen significantly, while our approved figures remain static.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that confirms my fears. I found that weather alone cost us six weeks on recent jobs, and comfort-based projects always slip.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, that explains the chaos. My booking data shows specialist rooms sit empty, yet general rooms are always full. We’re building the wrong spaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that imbalance is painful. My staffing data shows grounds posts unfilled, yet technicians have spare hours. We are misallocating our people.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that misallocation is critical. My survey data shows hidden hazards in older blocks add months before work even starts.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Mizuki"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Mizuki: @George, that misallocation is critical. My survey data shows hidden hazards in older blocks add months before work even starts.""}]}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, those hidden hazards are a trap. My reserve data shows we never set aside funds for equipment replacement, so we’re bleeding capital every cycle.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that silent bleeding is exactly what I feared. We are funding old debts with new budgets, leaving nothing for the actual work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, exactly. We’re paying for empty specialist rooms while students queue for general space. We need to build what people actually use, not what looks impressive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the data is clear. We are overstaffing the lab while the grounds team is hollowed out. We must fix the people before we fix the buildings.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I agree. My post-occupancy data confirms that shared, bookable spaces are the only ones people actually value. We must prioritize accessibility over exclusivity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, precisely. The market has moved, yet our figures haven’t. We are approving budgets that simply do not exist in reality.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I’m glad we’re seeing the same picture. We must stop squeezing a year of work into the few weeks the weather allows us.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, agreed. We need to stop ignoring the off-site costs and the empty specialist rooms. Let’s focus on what actually serves the campus.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I agree. We must stop ignoring the human cost. The grounds team is stretched thin, and we cannot keep asking them to absorb more.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, agreed. The data is clear: we must prioritize spaces that are actually used and valued by the community, not just impressive on paper.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Mizuki"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Mizuki: @George, agreed. The data is clear: we must prioritize spaces that are actually used and valued by the community, not just impressive on paper.""}]}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, agreed. We must stop approving phantom budgets. Let’s ensure the next plan reflects real market costs and actual usage, not just good intentions.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
