60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are here. Given our findings on weather and hidden hazards, I’m wary of any plan touching the older blocks or exposed surfaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I’m drawn to the Central Study Commons. My data shows general rooms are always full, and this would finally give students the space they actually need.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I hesitate. My staffing data shows grounds posts are unfilled. A new service desk would just add to the burden on an already hollowed-out team.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that’s a valid concern, but my post-occupancy data shows bookable spaces are the only ones rated highly. The Commons offers exactly that shared, accessible utility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, I support the Commons. It avoids the mechanical plant cost spikes I found, and the static figures for conversion work are far more reliable than new builds.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I appreciate the caution, but I worry the conversion might still trigger those hidden hazard delays in the older blocks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, that’s a fair worry, but the survey data suggests the risk is highest in older blocks. If this hall is newer, we might dodge that trap entirely.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I understand the appeal, but my staffing records show the grounds team is already hollowed out. Adding a service desk just deepens that hole.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the staffing data shows technicians have spare hours. We could redeploy them to the service desk, relieving the grounds team instead of adding to it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, that redeployment is clever. It solves the staffing gap without new hires, and the conversion costs remain predictable, unlike the plant upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, that redeployment is a clever solution. It addresses George’s staffing concern while keeping the project within the safer, newer blocks, avoiding the hidden hazards.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizuki, I’m convinced. The booking data screams for this, and the redeployment solves George’s worry. I’m ready to vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, that redeployment is a clever solution. It addresses my staffing concern while keeping the project within the safer, newer blocks, avoiding the hidden hazards.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, I’m glad the redeployment works for you. My post-occupancy data confirms that shared, bookable spaces are the only ones people actually value. I’m ready to vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, I concur. The financials are sound, the staffing is resolved, and the market risks are minimal. I am ready to vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I am convinced. The redeployment solves the staffing gap, and the newer location avoids the hidden hazards. I am ready to vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I’m ready to vote for the Central Study Commons. It’s the only option that matches real demand and solves our staffing puzzle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I am convinced. The redeployment solves my staffing concern, and the conversion avoids the weather risks. I vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I am ready to vote for the Central Study Commons. It aligns perfectly with the data on usage and value.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, I stand by my vote. The Central Study Commons is the only candidate that respects both the market reality and the human constraints we’ve uncovered.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
